cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Mirage humanoid perception benchmark: small detectors and VLMs on COCO-300, probes and visual questions"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible benchmark of small on-device perception models for a humanoid robot's
  perception layer: Cactus Mirage, YOLO26n, RF-DETR, D-FINE, RTMDet, OWLv2, Florence-2 and small
  vision-language models, on the same 300 COCO val2017 images, blank-frame and stability probes,
  synthetic signs and a frozen set of 254 visual questions, with laptop CPU/GPU latency.
type: software
